  "title": "",
  "body": "   When you have selected the t-statistic and the theory-based overlay, you can also use this applet for estimating the parameter of interest. (You can also go directly to the Theory-Based Inference applet which will also allow you to change the confidence level.) Check the box next to 95% CI(s) for difference in means .     Identify, in words related to the context of this study, the relevant parameter to be estimated here.    The difference in the average number of close friends between men and women in the U.S. population.      Report the 95% confidence interval for this parameter.    (-0.4100, -0.0454)      Does the 95% confidence interval calculated from the GSS sample data contain the value 0? What does that imply? (Hint: Recall that a confidence interval is an interval of plausible values for the parameter of interest, and the interval is calculated using the sample statistics.)    No, it does not contain zero, implying that a difference of zero between the two means (men and women) is not plausible.      Does the 95% confidence interval agree with your conclusion in ? How are you deciding?    Yes, we had evidence to reject the null hypothesis which stated that the two group means were the same; the small p-value gave us evidence that it's not plausible that the two group means are the same in the population, based on the evidence we have in our sample.      Fill in the blanks of the sentence to complete the interpretation of the 95% confidence interval:  We are ______% confident that the mean number of close friends men have is ______ than the mean number of close friends that women have, by between ______ and ______ friends.    95%; smaller; 0.0454; 0.4100.      How would the width of the interval change if you increased the confidence level to 99%? Why?    Increase, because you are more confident you ‘caught’ the parameter in the interval.      How would the width of the interval change if you increased the sample size? Why?    Decrease, because with an increased sample size you have more precision.      How would the width of the interval change if the variability of the number of close friends increased for both males and females? Why?    Increase, because with increased variability you have decreased precision.    "
