  "title": "",
  "body": "   Using a significance level of , do the data provide convincing evidence that the days of the week that women give birth are not equally distributed throughout the week?      State the hypotheses using either words or symbols        At least one is different.       Name the theory-based test you will use and verify validity conditions for that test.    The Chi-square goodness of fit test can be used, but only with simulation because validity conditions are not met to carry out a theory-based test.       Calculate the test statistic (standardized statistic) and corresponding p-value.    2.854, p-value = 0.844       State your conclusion (with appropriate justification based on your p-value and stated significance level) in the context of the research question.    There is weak evidence against the null because the p-value is much larger than the significance level of 0.05. It is plausible that birthdays are distributed equally over the seven days of the week.       If there is not sufficient evidence to support the research hypothesis that all seven days of the week are not equally likely to be birthdays, is this proof that birthdays are evenly distributed throughout the days of the week? Explain.    No, that is one plausible explanation for the data.       Were these data stronger or weaker evidence against the null hypothesis than the data you observed? Is this what you predicted?    Weaker; yes that is what was predicted.       Based on your conclusion in (d), are you potentially making a conclusion error? Explain the potential consequences of this type of error in this context.    It is possible that a Type II error was made, that is a false negative, or missed opportunity.    "
